      },
      "message": "fix(ui): another setup's WCS triad stays on its spot of the part\n\nWith two setups holding the part differently, the viewport drew the\nother setup's WCS at its raw stored place (in its own setup's frame),\noff the part. `setup_relative::wcs_view_pose` now maps it through\n`transform_between(owner, active)` - the transform the part itself\ngoes through - and the gizmo builder draws that pose; a refused\ntransform hides the triad instead of drawing it somewhere wrong. The\nactive setup's own WCS and setup-less documents are unchanged.\n\nPinned by wcs_view_pose (app, 3 tests) and\nwcs_gizmo_tests::another_setups_wcs_triad_rides_the_part_into_the_shown_setup\n(ui; fails with the mapping disabled).\n\nFixes #558\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
